 ## 10.3: Future Work
 
+## 10.4: MCP-style Integration
+
+UbU should be both an MCP-style client and server. Every tool surface is bounded by user-owned policy, Compartment rules, capability grants, and review semantics.
+
+### Client Capabilities
+
+UbU may connect to external tools and services through a structured API that:
+
+- Requires explicit capability grants
+- Enforces Compartment boundaries
+- Logs all tool calls and their outcomes
+- Supports rate limiting and cost tracking
+
+### Server Capabilities
+
+UbU may expose narrow capabilities to external agents through a bounded interface that:
+
+- Requires explicit authorization
+- Limits access scope to specific objects or operations
+- Enforces review semantics for all candidate updates
+- Supports audit trails and rollback mechanisms
+
+### Tool Call Semantics
+
+All external tool calls must be submitted as candidate updates rather than canonical writes. The planner, Logs, Compartment policy, and user-review rules decide what becomes canonical.
+
+### Security Boundaries
+
+The MCP integration must:
+
+- Prevent unauthorized access to user data
+- Ensure all external interactions are logged and auditable
+- Maintain user sovereignty over all decisions
+- Enforce Compartment policies at all interaction points
+
+This approach allows UbU to integrate with external systems while preserving its core principles of user control and privacy.
+
