+## 8. MCP Integration Contract
+
+This section defines the minimum contract for MCP-style integration within the planning kernel.
+
+### Tool Interface Requirements
+
+All external tools must be represented as capability-granted interfaces that:
+
+- Accept candidate updates rather than canonical writes
+- Enforce compartment boundaries
+- Provide provenance and confidence metadata
+- Support audit logging
+
+### Capability Grant Schema
+
+Each tool interface requires a capability grant with fields:
+
+- `object_scope`: specific object or subtree access
+- `operation_kind`: allowed operations
+- `compartment`: required compartment access
+- `identity`: required identity permissions
+- `time_window`: temporal scope
+- `rate_limit`: optional rate/cost limits
+- `review_required`: boolean flag
+
+### Tool Call Logging
+
+All tool calls must be logged with:
+
+- Timestamp
+- Tool identifier
+- Operation type
+- Request parameters
+- Response outcome
+- Audit trail reference
+
+### Candidate Update Semantics
+
+Tool calls produce candidate updates that are:
+
+- Not canonical until reviewed
+- Subject to compartment policy enforcement
+- Logged for audit
+- Reversible if needed
+
+This contract ensures that external integrations are bounded, auditable, and preserve user sovereignty.
+
